WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.176 --> 00:00:07.343
- Could diversity take away
from your creativity as well?

00:00:08.776 --> 00:00:11.443
- I think the critical thing is,

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.792
stay true to your idea,
stay true to your mission,

00:00:15.792 --> 00:00:19.173
your purpose, that's fundamental,
that's your foundation.

00:00:19.173 --> 00:00:21.997
But, within that, then the next questions,

00:00:21.997 --> 00:00:24.074
how do you reach your audience?

00:00:24.074 --> 00:00:26.025
And then also, how do you do it?

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:29.513
How do you get a market, how
do you create the product?

00:00:29.513 --> 00:00:32.945
I think by including
diversity you actually

00:00:32.945 --> 00:00:35.895
increase the level of
creativity dramatically.

00:00:35.895 --> 00:00:37.682
And the financial results of companies

00:00:37.682 --> 00:00:41.558
that are strong and diverse
tend to be way better

00:00:41.558 --> 00:00:46.248
than those that are very
restrictive and traditional.

00:00:46.248 --> 00:00:49.915
Now I think, why does
it increase diversity?

00:00:50.822 --> 00:00:52.376
Again, at Spotify it's really cool,

00:00:52.376 --> 00:00:56.002
they have this music
room and then they have

00:00:56.002 --> 00:00:57.817
this area where they can watch people

00:00:57.817 --> 00:01:00.285
on focus groups and stuff like that.

00:01:00.285 --> 00:01:02.115
And they deliberately
will get very diverse

00:01:02.115 --> 00:01:04.787
people listening to their new products.

00:01:04.787 --> 00:01:06.777
And actually going through
the whole usability

00:01:06.777 --> 00:01:08.610
of their new products.

00:01:09.952 --> 00:01:12.802
I guess I've lived in
technology a long time,

00:01:12.802 --> 00:01:16.969
you cannot believe how great
engineers don't realize

00:01:17.812 --> 00:01:20.283
how difficult to use their products are.

00:01:20.283 --> 00:01:22.304
And they might have
built the best mouse trap

00:01:22.304 --> 00:01:23.593
in the world, they might have built

00:01:23.593 --> 00:01:25.445
the best features of functions with

00:01:25.445 --> 00:01:28.757
the coolest kinds of music
download in the world,

00:01:28.757 --> 00:01:32.140
but unless it's usable
and simple and intuitive,

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:35.486
then it's not going to get the air time.

00:01:35.486 --> 00:01:38.736
So you never ever ever get disappointed

00:01:42.164 --> 00:01:46.704
by getting user feedback in
terms of (mumbles) products.

00:01:46.704 --> 00:01:49.596
And I think around that you
don't just want to (mumbles)

00:01:49.596 --> 00:01:51.497
unless you've got a very narrow product,

00:01:51.497 --> 00:01:53.848
just to one segment of society.

00:01:53.848 --> 00:01:56.936
It's much better if you really
want to scale your product

00:01:56.936 --> 00:02:00.552
to do that and then go
out to other segments

00:02:00.552 --> 00:02:02.365
and be very diverse in your thinking.

00:02:02.365 --> 00:02:06.495
I think the creativity, just
speaking from me personally,

00:02:06.495 --> 00:02:09.753
by having a lot of
people within the company

00:02:09.753 --> 00:02:12.989
challenge me, from very
diverse backgrounds,

00:02:12.989 --> 00:02:15.954
gives me a much greater
appreciation of how to do

00:02:15.954 --> 00:02:18.679
the best for our customers.

00:02:18.679 --> 00:02:21.425
And again it's so true in life.

00:02:21.425 --> 00:02:22.918
Sometimes I think as an entrepreneur,

00:02:22.918 --> 00:02:27.008
you get a bit successful, you
stop believing your own PR

00:02:27.008 --> 00:02:28.573
and you get a bit comfortable.

00:02:28.573 --> 00:02:32.080
And when you do that, you
kind of lose your creativity.

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:34.527
Whereas, what your
questions all about Kirk,

00:02:34.527 --> 00:02:38.153
is about how do you
accelerate that creativity.

00:02:38.153 --> 00:02:40.339
Now I think diversity
is just one of the ways

00:02:40.339 --> 00:02:44.616
you could do that and
get some fantastic input.

00:02:44.616 --> 00:02:48.121
Really strong invention in a (mumbles).

00:02:48.121 --> 00:02:50.402
And then as a leader, you kind
of got to make the choices

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:54.374
and start executing them,
delivering on that vision.

00:02:54.374 --> 00:02:57.048
- Yeah I'm definitely
with Steven on this one.

00:02:57.048 --> 00:02:58.968
I don't know that we really disagree a lot

00:02:58.968 --> 00:03:00.783
on the questions anyway,
just different sides

00:03:00.783 --> 00:03:03.023
of the coin on most of these.

00:03:03.023 --> 00:03:06.986
I don't see a world in
which for any company,

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:09.720
adding diversity would
take away from creativity.

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:11.875
Just I don't know how that happens.

00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:16.233
I think maybe your own,
if you're injecting other

00:03:16.233 --> 00:03:19.371
people into a company then
maybe the responsibility

00:03:19.371 --> 00:03:22.233
on you isn't as great to be creative.

00:03:22.233 --> 00:03:24.370
If you have to come up with everything,

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.123
then now that you have people,

00:03:26.123 --> 00:03:27.673
you can rely on maybe
you don't have to come up

00:03:27.673 --> 00:03:31.629
with as many ideas, maybe
your own personal creativity.

00:03:31.629 --> 00:03:32.930
I don't know if that's
what he's getting at.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.701
But look at what's in the
best interest of your company.

00:03:36.701 --> 00:03:38.865
The best ideas win.

00:03:38.865 --> 00:03:40.862
If it's only you coming up with ideas

00:03:40.862 --> 00:03:44.525
and the ideas are just
okay, by adding more people

00:03:44.525 --> 00:03:48.801
into the mix, they can take
that okay idea into a great one.

00:03:48.801 --> 00:03:50.998
And so, if that means
you're not coming up with

00:03:50.998 --> 00:03:52.982
every single idea for the business,

00:03:52.982 --> 00:03:54.389
then maybe that's a good thing to help you

00:03:54.389 --> 00:03:56.722
get to where you need to go.

